    "Description": "## Summary\n\n`sanitize-html` discards the *content* of every element in `nonTextTags`. It delimits that region\nusing htmlparser2's close events, and ignores the `isImplied` flag htmlparser2 passes it. Closing a\nstill-open **ancestor** from inside a `\u003cnoscript\u003e` makes htmlparser2 unwind its stack past the\n`noscript`; the synthetic implied close it emits on the way ends the discard region early, and\neverything after it is treated as ordinary body content.\n\nA browser with scripting enabled parses `\u003cnoscript\u003e` content as **raw text**, so the same markup\nrenders as inert text there. The sanitizer therefore emits elements the page itself would not have.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```js\nconst sanitizeHtml = require(\"sanitize-html\");\n\nsanitizeHtml('\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cnoscript\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg src=\"http://evil.test/t.gif\"\u003e\u003c/noscript\u003e', {\n  allowedTags: [\"div\", \"img\"],\n  allowedAttributes: { img: [\"src\"] },\n  nonTextTags: [\"script\", \"style\", \"textarea\", \"option\", \"noscript\"],\n});\n// =\u003e '\u003cdiv\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg src=\"http://evil.test/t.gif\" /\u003e'\n```\n\nChrome, given the same input, renders **no** `\u003cimg\u003e` — the whole payload is raw text inside the\nunclosed `\u003cnoscript\u003e`. Verified with Playwright, `srcdoc` into an iframe so the scripting flag is on.\n\nA `\u003c![CDATA[` variant hides the opening tag from the parser entirely and has the same effect:\n\n```\n\u003cp\u003eHi\u003c/p\u003e\u003c![CDATA[ x \u003e \u003cnoscript\u003e]]\u003e\u003ca href=\"…\"\u003eReset your password\u003c/a\u003e\u003cimg src=\"…beacon.gif\"\u003e\u003c/noscript\u003e\n```\n\nhtmlparser2 runs a CDATA token to `]]\u003e`; Chrome ends a bogus comment at the first `\u003e`, so the\n`\u003cnoscript\u003e` after it is real to the browser and invisible to the parser.\n\n## Where the behaviour is\n\n`index.js`:\n\n- `:154` — `nonTextTagsArray` (the default list, `['script','style','textarea','option','xmp']`).\n- `:638` — `onclosetag: function (name, isImplied)` — receives the flag.\n- `:644` — `skipTextDepth--` — decrements without consulting `isImplied`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nDo not end a discard region on an implied close. htmlparser2 already distinguishes them; the flag\nis passed and discarded. Something close to:\n\n```js\nonclosetag: function (name, isImplied) {\n  if (skipText) {\n    if (isImplied) return;   // an implied close must not end the region\n    skipTextDepth--;\n    …\n```",
